## 🚗 EV Control

The EV control module manages the basic vehicle operating parameters.

### Drive Modes

Three drive modes are supported:

| Mode   | Torque            |
| ------ | ----------------- |
| ECO    | 0.6 × base torque |
| NORMAL | 1.0 × base torque |
| SPORT  | 1.3 × base torque |

The system also handles:

* Accelerator input
* Brake input
* Motor torque
* Vehicle speed
* Regenerative braking
* Battery SOC
* Motor temperature
* Estimated driving range

---

## 🛡️ ADAS Features

### 1. Forward Collision Warning

The front ultrasonic sensor is used to detect obstacles.

Warning conditions:

```text
Distance < 50 cm
OR
TTC < 3 seconds
```

Critical conditions:

```text
Distance < 20 cm
OR
TTC < 1.5 seconds
```

The system uses hysteresis to prevent rapid warning ON/OFF switching.

---

### 2. Time-to-Collision (TTC)

TTC is calculated using:

```text
TTC = Distance / Vehicle Speed
```

Vehicle speed is converted from km/h to m/s before calculating TTC.

When the vehicle is stationary or no relevant obstacle is detected, TTC is treated as safe.

---

### 3. Blind Spot Detection

Left and right ultrasonic sensors are used for blind-spot monitoring.

A blind-spot warning is generated when:

```text
Obstacle distance < 30 cm
AND
Vehicle speed > 20 km/h
```

Separate detection is provided for:

* Left blind spot
* Right blind spot

---

### 4. Alarm Priority

The system supports four alarm levels:

```text
NONE
ADVISORY
WARNING
CRITICAL
```

Priority:

```text
CRITICAL
   ↓
WARNING
   ↓
ADVISORY
   ↓
NONE
```

